      <h2>Africa's Gold Mining Equipment Guide</h2>
      <p>Africa is home to some of the world's richest gold deposits, from the Democratic Republic of Congo's alluvial fields to Zimbabwe's ancient reef systems. After supplying wash plants to operations across the continent, we've learned what works in African conditions — and what doesn't. Here's your complete guide to choosing the right equipment for African gold mining operations.</p>
      
      <h3>Most Popular Models for African Operations</h3>
      <p>Based on our shipments to DRC, Zimbabwe, Mozambique, and other African countries, certain models consistently outperform others:</p>
      
      <p><strong><a href="/products/50-ton/">M50 Gold Wash Plant</a> — The African Favorite:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Why it's popular:</strong> Ships in one 20' container, easy to transport to remote sites</li>
        <li><strong>Capacity:</strong> 50 tons per hour — perfect for small to medium alluvial deposits</li>
        <li><strong>Power:</strong> 75 HP — manageable with generator power</li>
        <li><strong>Shipping cost:</strong> Lowest per unit, fits in standard container</li>
        <li><strong>Site requirements:</strong> Minimal preparation needed</li>
      </ul>
      
      <p><strong><a href="/products/100-ton/">M100 Gold Wash Plant</a> — The Growing Choice:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Why chosen:</strong> Good balance of capacity and shipping costs</li>
        <li><strong>Capacity:</strong> 100 tons per hour — handles larger deposits efficiently</li>
        <li><strong>Power:</strong> 100 HP — still generator-friendly</li>
        <li><strong>Shipping:</strong> One 40' container — reasonable freight costs</li>
        <li><strong>ROI:</strong> Better economics for medium-scale operations</li>
      </ul>

