    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <h3>What's the most popular wash plant model for African mining operations?</h3>
    <p>The M50 wash plant is most popular in Africa because it ships in one 20' container, has the lowest shipping costs, requires minimal site preparation, and works well with generator power for remote locations.</p>

    <h3>What are the main challenges for gold mining equipment in Africa?</h3>
    <p>Key challenges include poor road access, lack of grid power (requiring generators), limited water infrastructure, complex import procedures, seasonal accessibility during rainy seasons, and need for self-sufficient operations.</p>

    <h3>Which African ports are best for importing mining equipment?</h3>
    <p>Best ports include Durban (South Africa) for excellent infrastructure, Tema (Ghana) for West Africa, Dar es Salaam (Tanzania) for East Africa, and Maputo (Mozambique) for southern African distribution.</p>

    <h3>What power requirements should I plan for in African mining?</h3>
    <p>Size the generator above the plant's draw rather than to it, budget 3-5 gallons of diesel per hour, and always keep a backup on site since downtime is expensive. We confirm the power package with you per order.</p>

    <h3>How much should I budget for total cost of ownership in Africa?</h3>
    <p>Budget: 40-50% equipment cost, 10-15% shipping, 15-20% site prep, 10-15% power infrastructure, 5-10% water infrastructure, plus 6 months working capital for operations.</p>
